  "title": "Plague of Justinian",
  "summary": "Procopius placed the start of the plague at Pelusium in Egypt, from where it spread to Alexandria, Palestine and, in 542, Constantinople. Procopius reported nearly 10,000 deaths a day in the capital, which modern historians put nearer 5,000. Maximalist estimates cited in a modelling study run to a quarter to half of the Eastern Roman Empire, or 15 to 100 million people.",
